; ---------------------------------------------------------
; VNKit 2.12.1 — Phone Gameplay Loop demo
; The full gameplay loop in one script:
;   message received → read → player doesn't answer →
;   Contacts → character card → Chat Action → affection changes →
;   photo received → photo viewed → Notes → Schedule → Phone Game →
;   game result into a variable → message expires → character reacts.
; Enable "Use Placeholder Graphics" to run this without any art.
; ---------------------------------------------------------

# Start

@bg Campus time:0.8
@bgm ThemeDay fade:1.5
@phoneOn
@set affection.rin=0, trust.rin=0, reliability.rin=0

Classes are over. Tomorrow is the entrance test for the «Elysium» program —
and Rin has been digging through the academy archive all week.

; --- Two chats already exist: Max (plain history) and Rin.
; Rin's message carries id:rin_elysium — from now on the script can check
; message.rin_elysium.received / .read / .answered (and later .expired).
@msg chat:max notify:0 from:"Max" "Yo. Music club after classes, you in?"
@msg chat:rin notify:0 from:"Rin" "Found something in the archive. About «Elysium»."
@msg chat:rin id:rin_elysium from:"Rin" "Roof. Six o'clock. Tell me you'll be there."

; --- The archive photo goes to the gallery LOCKED: the player sees
; a dimmed tile but can't open it until the script unlocks it.
@gallery add cg/roof_sky id:roof1 locked:1 sender:"Rin" date:"May 12" location:"Roof" desc:"A page from the academy archive." tag:elysium

; --- Both contacts come online; Rin has a live dialogue waiting.
@online chat:max contact:"Max 🎧" goto:MaxTalk notify:0
@online chat:rin contact:"Rin 🌸" goto:RinTalk

; --- Contextual actions for Rin's chat. They are reachable from the chat
; itself AND from her card in Contacts (Contacts → Rin → action).
; do: changes relationship variables; once:1 (default) makes each action
; fire only once — even across Save/Load and Rollback.
@chatActions chat:rin "Ask about the archive" goto:AskArchive do:affection.rin+=1 | "Promise to come" goto:Promise do:reliability.rin+=1

Rin's dot lights up online. Open the phone (RMB): read her message,
check Contacts — her card shows affection / trust / reliability and
the same action buttons as the chat.

; --- FREE PHONE PHASE: the script parks here until «Continue».
; The player may answer Rin — or ignore her.
@phonehub

; --- Did the player answer the tracked message?
@if message.rin_elysium.answered == true goto:WasAnswered
You never answered Rin's message. She noticed.
@set reliability.rin-=1
@goto AfterHub

# WasAnswered
You answered — that's worth something to her.
@set trust.rin+=1

# AfterHub

; --- Evening: Rin sends the archive photo. The gallery entry unlocks,
; and the photo lands in the chat as a tracked message too.
@msg chat:rin from:"Rin" "Here. Straight from the archive."
@gallery unlock id:roof1
@photo chat:rin cg/roof_sky sender:Rin id:rin_photo

Check the Gallery — the locked tile is open now. Tap the photo:
left click zooms in, the wheel zooms smoothly, drag to pan.

; --- Second free phase: let the player actually look at the photo.
@phonehub

; --- Did the player VIEW the photo? (gallery.roof1.viewed == true)
@if gallery.roof1.viewed == true goto:SawPhoto
You never opened the photo. Whatever was on that page — you missed it.
@goto AfterPhoto

# SawPhoto
You studied every line of the archive page. This goes into Notes —
as evidence, with the source attached.
@note add "The archive page mentions the «Elysium» selection program." id:n1 category:evidence source:rin
@note add "Rin has archive access. How?" id:n2 category:secrets source:rin

# AfterPhoto

; --- Notes + Schedule as ordinary gameplay tools.
@note add "Max invited me to the music club." id:n3 category:people source:max
@schedule add time:"18:00" title:"Roof — meeting with Rin" id:ev1
@schedule add time:"21:00" title:"Dorm curfew" id:ev2

; --- PHONE GAME: the result lands in a variable (and in
; phoneGame.Lockpick.plays / .last for the Games tab).
On the way home — the old storage room. The padlock opens like a phone app.
@phoneGame Lockpick var:lockResult
@if lockResult == 1 goto:Cracked
The pick broke. (lockResult = 0, phoneGame.Lockpick.last = 0.)
@goto AfterGame

# Cracked
Unlocked! (lockResult = 1.) Inside — a dusty folder stamped «ELYSIUM».
@note add "Storage room: a folder stamped «ELYSIUM»." id:n4 category:evidence source:player

# AfterGame

; --- EXPIRE: the six-o'clock invitation is no longer relevant.
; Not a timer — a plain script state: message.rin_elysium.expired = 1.
@message expire id:rin_elysium

; --- The character reacts: the follow-up depends on affection AND on
; whether the message expired unanswered.
@if affection.rin >= 2 goto:WarmRin
@msg chat:rin from:"Rin" "You could at least pretend to be interested."
@goto Finale

# WarmRin
@msg chat:rin from:"Rin" "…thanks for today. For listening. For everything."

# Finale

Everything you saw — message states, the gallery lock, viewed photos,
notes with categories, the schedule, chat actions, game stats — lives
in the save file and survives rollback.

@phoneOff
@end

; ---------------------------------------------------------
# RinTalk
Rin: You're online! Did you read it?
{playerName}: Just opened the chat.
@typing time:1.4
Rin: Six o'clock. Roof. Don't be late — this is about «Elysium».
@typing time:1.0
Rin: And… thanks for not ignoring me.
@chatend

# MaxTalk
Max: Yooo, {playerName}! Music club, you coming?
{playerName}: Maybe later. Things to do.
@typing time:1.1
Max: You and your secrets 😑
@chatend

# AskArchive
{playerName}: Tell me about the archive. What did you find?
@typing time:1.6
Rin: A whole section on the «Elysium» program. Selection, tests, contracts…
Rin: I'll send you the photo tonight. Don't show anyone.
@chatend

# Promise
{playerName}: I'll be there at six. Promise.
@typing time:0.9
Rin: You'd better be.
@chatend
